# #327 bbt-rt test sweep

Brief 46f7fa1e-e63e-40dd-9c26-aa83e9285536; night rules 3c2df395 and 452c9ada; fresh base fb36df74a808029ba9f1de07c0f181772fe04077.
Scope: tests/cfg(test), the minimal caller-controlled release seam in fault.rs, append-only exact night selectors. No production command/cancellation/wake policy changed. The existing timed fault wrapper still starts its tokio delay after IO readiness.
The overlap scan found only Nyx's old clean frozen R5i verify tree, not an active RT edit; current Nyx claims are supervisor tests and landing scripts. No peer in-flight RT file excluded.

Before: 23 registered/default tests, 23/0/0 ignored; reported binary times sum 2.22 s. After: 22 registered, default 19/0 + 3 named night cases excluded; reported default binary times sum 0.02 s. Each exact night case passed individually (1/0 each). This is a default-tier reduction, not a native speed-gate claim. The manual night-boundary probes ran alongside ordinary machine work; throughput/latency are diagnostic samples, not controlled-load acceptance.
3 explicit Rust sleep calls removed, plus elapsed-time spins/polls. No sleep or wall-clock speed assertion remains in the default tests. All remaining recv_timeout calls are 120 s hang guards. Existing synthetic meter timestamps stay unchanged. Four original native functions remain intact as assertions inside one named real_process_boundary; count consolidation removes no native behavior coverage.

