New default contracts: a_full_queue_returns_the_original_message_without_consumption checks the exact rejected message and retained original, independent of throughput. held_file_read_allows_exact_ui_messages_before_release receives IO-ready, proves the read stays pending while 100 exact UiMsg values pass, releases it, and checks native bytes plus zero blocking-guard violations. Separate binaries own their UI registration, so no process-wide UI thread race was introduced.

Coverage map: runtime §1/§2 -> singleton/IO guard and controlled handoff; §3 -> bounded queue/ring/latest, dirty wake/retained/deferred tail and 100k concurrent delivery; native argv/cwd/env/stdout/stderr/exit/cancel/spawn failures -> real_process_boundary; §5 -> synthetic hitch windows/idle gaps, disabled clocks, bounded counter/probe and callback accounting; §6 -> controlled read default proof plus exact two-second native night measurement. Every kept libtest is tagged. No invariant check command or spec acceptance line deleted.

Native completion waits drain the existing DirtySet and wait on its Waker signal, never a sleep. The cancellation assertion observes a descendant only after root wait and both inherited pipe EOFs complete. Its hour-long fixture lifetime exceeds the 120 s hang guard, preventing natural termination from hiding a failed kill. CancelOnDrop retires only its fixture-created TaskId group on failure.

Night dispatch is scripts/night-boundaries.d/bbt-rt.sh, three exact selectors with --test-threads=1. The shared dispatcher remains byte-identical to the accepted per-crate split; no existing selector changed and no blanket --ignored run was added. sh -n scripts/night-boundaries.d/bbt-rt.sh, sh -n scripts/night-test-boundaries.sh and git diff --check EXIT0. Strict Clippy and affected invariants are the combined author presubmit, not duplicated prechecks.

